      "rationale": "ECI: Epoch's frontier stood at 162.5 (Claude Fable 5) on 2026-08-21, but GPT-6 Astra (released 2026-09-03) scores 169 on Epoch's index. Epoch measures the reasoning-era frontier advancing ~14 pts/yr; realized 6-month gains since 2024 have run +7 to +17 (median ~+9-10), with four labs shipping flagships weekly and explicit RSI pushes at Google/OpenAI, partly offset by voluntary RL-training pauses and capability-gating of top models (Mythos, restricted Astra tiers). Hence median ~178.5 by 2027-03-08, with fat upside. Incident ladder: the low rungs are already effectively realized \u2014 IBM's 2026 report finds 1 in 4 malicious breaches AI-enabled at ~$6M average, FBI/IC3 logged $893M of AI-attributed US losses in 2025, CSO put global AI-related losses near $30B, and identifiable campaigns (ShinyHunters' AI-vishing/OAuth abuse across 1,000+ orgs, Iran-linked AI-accelerated OT attacks, CISA's AI-generated PLC exploit advisories) plus the OpenAI eval-agent breach of Hugging Face give near-certainty at $220M and high probability at $2.2B, so I put cyber/AI 100- and 1k-rungs at 0.85-0.99 within 12 months. Middle rungs are anchored on FRI's July 2026 pilot (5-8% for a \u2265$10B data-damaging worm in 2026, rising 3-3.5x under AI-enabled elite exploit development) and FRI LEAP Wave 9 (62-70% for a \u226550-death/\u2265$100B AI harm event by 2050; 25% by 2031), tempered because those forecasters clearly read \"event\" restrictively while these questions permit cumulation across incidents. Tail rungs and the catastrophe questions lean on XPT (AI catastrophe by 2100: 2.1% superforecasters, 12% AI experts; total catastrophe 9%/20%) and LEAP Wave 9's AI-catastrophe path (0.08%/1%/2% slow vs 1%/5%/10% rapid by 2030/2050/2100); today's world reads closer to \"rapid,\" so I blend to ~0.6%/4%/8% for catastrophe:ai and ~1%/5.5%/11% for catastrophe:general, with disempowerment at 1.7%/13%/24%. Bio stays much lower than cyber near-term (no AI-enabled epidemic has occurred; barriers remain acquisition/production) but rises materially by 2050-2100 given AI-designed replicating viruses, screening evasion by generative protein design, and labs' own inability to rule out novice uplift. Conditions: policy effects are scaled by horizon (near-zero at 6-12 months, full by 2050), by severity rung, and by how much the cause depends on US developer behavior \u2014 so p1/sq raise risk modestly, p2a/p3a/p4 cut it 10-25% at full strength, p2b/p3b cut 35-40%, and the P5 bundle cuts 55% (largest for misalignment and disempowerment, smallest for criminal cyber, diluted for catastrophe:general by non-AI pathways). Capability conditions move tail rungs most (p90 \u2248 1.5-2.5x, p10 \u2248 0.4-0.6x at 2028-2030) and attenuate toward 2100, since a single 2027 snapshot says less about end-of-century outcomes.",
